23
00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.860 line:15%
If you're gonna buy one piece of equipment for baking,

24
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.690 line:15%
I say it's the scale.

25
00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.600
It's all about consistency,

26
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.590
and weighing your ingredients makes all the difference.

27
00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.590
If you want your batches to be the same

28
00:01:04.590 --> 00:01:08.490
over and over and over again, use a kitchen scale.

29
00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.250
Measuring flour in a measuring cup

30
00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.800
can weigh different things every time

31
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.940
depending on how you do it.

32
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.400
If you scoop and sweep versus spoon and sweep,

33
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.150
it's gonna be a different amount of flour each time,

34
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.670
whereas when you weigh one pound of flour,

35
00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.920
it's always gonna be one pound of flour.

36
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.533
If you do use measuring cups,

37
00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.173
make sure when you're measuring your flour,

38
00:01:32.173 --> 00:01:36.090
you'll put your flour in, sweep it level.

39
00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:38.765
The same is true for measuring spoons.

40
00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.540
You don't wanna dip it in there and have it heaping over.

41
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.160
You wanna level it off.

42
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.750
So these are the essentials

43
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.733
for measuring your dry ingredients.

44
