45
00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.210
You can grow mint in the ground,

46
00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.910 line:15%
but this is where we have our disclaimer for mint.

47
00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.240 line:15%
Mint is a very aggressively growing plant.

48
00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.940 line:15%
That means that where you plant mint,

49
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.240
it will expand and it will pop up all over your garden.

50
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:05.700
So my tip for you in growing mint

51
00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:10.377
is to either grow it in a pot or grow it in a raised bed.

52
00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:15.146
If you don't want to dedicate a whole raised bed to mint,

53
00:02:15.146 --> 00:02:20.146
you can actually bury a pot in the soil,

54
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.910
and that will help keep mint in this area.

55
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.320
We're gonna take your pot

56
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.270
and your pot can be as big as you want.

57
00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.370
If you want a bigger section of mint,

58
00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.540 line:15%
if it's at soil level,

59
00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.940 line:15%
those runners would expand right across the soil.

60
00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:35.820 line:15%
So you wanna leave it high up, keeping your mint in check

61
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:37.380 line:15%
if you don't want it to take over.

62
